invariant: INV-13
file: src/tcp_read.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: ch_read_in_place fails the session when the caller holds less than
  the next whole record, so a caller that has no record yet loses the
  session. INV-13 makes CH_TCP_AGAIN a result that is not an error, and a
  caller that read a ticket-only record would have to hold it back until
  a data record arrived (docs/decisions.md entries 46 and 247).

--- old
    if (rc == CH_OK || rc == CH_TCP_AGAIN || rc == CH_ECLOSED) {
        return rc;
    }
--- new
    if (rc == CH_OK || rc == CH_ECLOSED) {
        return rc;
    }
